{"step_index":278,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:40:39Z","thinking":"The user needs a practical, runnable code example contrasting the behavior of `const string&`. This requires constructing code snippets to demonstrate how `const` prevents modification and the reference avoids copying. An analogy is also required to reinforce the concept. I'll need to create code that modifies a string in one case, and show how `const string&` prevents that modification in another, illustrating the difference and the benefit of using a reference.\n\n\nConsider a C++ example using an ID card analogy to illustrate pass-by-value, pass-by-reference, and `const` with a reference.  The \"inspect\" function creates a copy of the ID, while \"eraseName\" directly modifies the original card (pass-by-reference). \"safePrint\" uses a `const` reference, allowing reading but preventing modification.  The code demonstrates the compiler's behavior, showing errors when trying to alter the `const` reference, and contrasting this with modifiable references and copies.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/ashutosh-goyal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/test_const_ref.cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\n// 1. Pass-by-Value: Makes a copy (wastes memory for big strings)\nvoid demoCopy(string s) {\n    s = \"Changed inside function\";\n}\n\n// 2. Pass-by-Reference: Modifies the original!\nvoid demoModify(string& s) {\n    s = \"Changed original!\";\n}\n\n// 3. const Reference: Fast (no copy) + Protected (cannot be changed)\nvoid demoSafeRead(const string& s) {\n    cout << \"Reading: \" << s << endl;\n    // s = \"Error!\"; // If you uncomment this, g++ refuses to compile!\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string my_name = \"Ashutosh\";\n\n    demoCopy(my_name);\n    cout << \"After demoCopy: \" << my_name << endl; // Still \"Ashutosh\"\n\n    demoModify(my_name);\n    cout << \"After demoModify: \" << my_name << endl; // Now \"Changed original!\"\n\n    demoSafeRead(my_name);\n\n    return 0;\n}\nEOF\ng++ -std=c++17 /home/ashutosh-goyal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/test_const_ref.cpp -o /home/ashutosh-goyal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/test_const_ref\n/home/ashutosh-goyal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/test_const_ref\n","Cwd":"/home/ashutosh-goyal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Compiling and running practical const and reference demo","toolSummary":"Run const & code demo"}}]}
